#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:0
msgid ""
"Use Orca commands to browse web pages, read in caret mode, check formatting, "
"fill forms, read tables and follow live regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:7
msgid "Topics: Accessibility"
msgstr "話題：無障礙功能"

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:11
msgid "Read documents and web pages using the screen reader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:13
msgid ""
"You can use the following screen reader commands to browse web pages, read "
"longer text documents and navigate tables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:15
msgid ""
"To start the screen reader and learn its basic control, go to {ref}`get-"
"started-with-the-screen-reader`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:19
msgid ""
"Ubuntu Desktop might present some challenges when using the screen reader. "
"If you experience difficulty, refer to {ref}`improve-screen-reader-"
"usability`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:20
msgid "Read documents using caret mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:22
msgid ""
"In caret mode, also known as caret browsing or caret navigation, you "
"navigate a document using the text cursor (caret). You move the cursor using "
"the arrow keys. As you navigate within the text of the document, Orca "
"presents your current location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:24
msgid "Enable caret navigation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:26
msgid ""
"Applications with text input, such as text editors and word processors, "
"enable caret navigation by default. The caret is the text cursor that you "
"use to enter text in the window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:27
msgid ""
"In many GNOME applications and in web browser such as Firefox and Chrome, "
"you can enable caret navigation by pressing {kbd}`F7`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:28
msgid "For other applications, consult their documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:30
msgid "Read the document using caret navigation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:32
msgid "Use {kbd}`Left` and {kbd}`Right` to move and read by character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:33
msgid "Use {kbd}`Ctrl+Left` and {kbd}`Ctrl+Right` to move and read by word."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:34
msgid "Use {kbd}`Up` and {kbd}`Down` to move and read by line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:35
msgid ""
"Use {kbd}`Shift` in combination with the previous commands to select and "
"unselect text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:37
msgid ""
"To read, spell, and obtain the Unicode value for the current text, refer to "
"{ref}`orca-examine-a-window`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:40
msgid "Read the entire document"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:42
msgid "Read the whole document from your cursor position to the end:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:0
msgid "Laptop layout"
msgstr "筆記型電腦配置"

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:49
msgid "{kbd}`CapsLock+;`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:0
msgid "Desktop layout"
msgstr "桌上型電腦配置"

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:55
msgid "{kbd}`Insert+;`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:58
msgid ""
"This is similar to the Say All command described in {ref}`orca-examine-a-"
"window`. However, Say All reads the whole window including buttons and other "
"interface elements, and it's limited to the currently visible content with "
"no hierarchy. In contrast, reading the entire document respects more complex "
"structure on web pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:61
msgid "Examine text formatting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:63
msgid ""
"Let Orca speak the text attributes of the current object, such as the font, "
"style, alignment, and other formatting associated with the given characters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:70
#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:96
msgid "{kbd}`CapsLock+F`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:76
#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:102
msgid "{kbd}`Insert+F`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:79
msgid "Preferences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:81
msgid ""
"The number of text attributes is large. You can customize which text "
"attributes Orca presents in speech, along with the order in which Orca lists "
"them. Optionally, Orca can indicate text attributes in braille by "
"\"underlining\" them as you navigate a document. Go to the {guilabel}`Text "
"Attributes` page of the Orca preferences dialog to change these settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:83
msgid ""
"You can also customize text attribute presentation for each application that "
"you use in the application-specific settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:85
msgid "Identify misspelled words"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:87
msgid "You can learn about spelling issues in several ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:89
msgid ""
"When you examine text formatting, Orca also announces spelling issues as one "
"of the text attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:105
msgid ""
"Orca recognizes the spelling issue by reading the underline formatting that "
"applications use to mark errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:107
msgid ""
"Enable key echo or word echo. When you misspell a word, Orca announces "
"\"misspelled\" so that you can immediately go back and correct the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:109
msgid ""
"When you move the caret into a word that's misspelled, Orca announces the "
"presence of the spelling error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:111
msgid ""
"Perform detailed Where Am I to learn more details about the spelling issue:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:118
msgid "{kbd}`CapsLock` + double-press {kbd}`Enter`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:124
msgid "{kbd}`Insert` + double-press {kbd}`Enter`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:129
msgid "Navigate the document structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:131
msgid ""
"The Structural Navigation feature enables you to browse elements in a "
"document. The types of elements by which you can navigate include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:133
msgid "Headings and other text blocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:134
msgid "Form controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:135
msgid "Links"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:136
msgid "Lists and list items"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:137
msgid "Landmarks, separators and anchors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:138
msgid "Tables and table cells"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:140
msgid "Structural Navigation is available in the following environments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:142
msgid "On **web pages**, you can navigate the full range of elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:143
msgid ""
"In **LibreOffice Writer** and OpenOffice Writer, you can navigate table "
"cells."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:145
msgid "Navigate a web page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:147
msgid ""
"On web pages, you usually read the content without editing it. You can use "
"the Structural Navigation commands directly. Refer to {ref}`orca-structural-"
"navigation-commands`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:149
msgid "Navigate elements in a text editor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:151
msgid ""
"In editable documents, such as those in **LibreOffice Writer** or an "
"**online text editor**, pressing letters on the keyboard types text in the "
"editor. Enable Structural Navigation to use letters as navigation shortcuts "
"instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:158
msgid "{kbd}`CapsLock+Z`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:164
msgid "{kbd}`Insert+Z`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:167
msgid "Browse elements using Structural Navigation commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:169
msgid "On web pages, refer to {ref}`orca-structural-navigation-commands`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:170
msgid ""
"In Writer, you can only use the commands for {ref}`orca-structural-"
"navigation-commands-tables`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:172
msgid ""
"To go back to writing, disable Structural Navigation using the same shortcut "
"that enables it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:175
msgid "Read tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:177
msgid ""
"Orca provides several features to access tables on web pages and in other "
"documents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:179
msgid "Read the cell or the row"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:181
msgid ""
"Consider the list of **messages in your Inbox**. To hear the sender, "
"subject, date and presence of attachments, you want Orca to **speak the "
"row**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:183
msgid ""
"On the other hand, consider the **rows in a spreadsheet**. You might not "
"want to hear the full row because of the large number of cells in each row. "
"In that case, you want Orca to only **speak the cell with focus**. Similar "
"situations occur in document tables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:185
msgid "You can switch between cell and row reading for the current table:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:192
msgid "{kbd}`CapsLock+F11`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:198
msgid "{kbd}`Insert+F11`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:201
msgid ""
"You can customize whether Orca reads the cell or the full row by default. "
"You can also choose different table reading modes for each type of table and "
"for specific applications. To edit the options, go to the {guilabel}`Speech` "
"page of Orca preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:203
msgid "Structural Navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:205
msgid ""
"With Structural Navigation commands, you can locate tables, jump to the "
"first or last cell and move to the next cell in any direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:207
msgid ""
"As you navigate the table, Orca announces the details about your position, "
"such as the dimensions of the table or that you have reached the edge of the "
"table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:209
msgid "For details, refer to {ref}`orca-navigate-the-document-structure`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:211
msgid "Mark a row or column as a header"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:213
msgid ""
"Many tables have incorrectly marked headers. A row or column often serves as "
"a header but it only uses bold or large text instead of semantic markup. In "
"other cases, the header might be correct but the application or the toolkit "
"don't provide the information to the screen reader."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:215
msgid ""
"In those cases, you can manually mark a row or column as a header using the "
"Dynamic Header feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:217
msgid "Set a row as a header"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:219
msgid "Tell Orca that the current row is the one with the headers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:226
msgid "{kbd}`CapsLock+R`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:232
msgid "{kbd}`Insert+R`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:235
msgid "Set a column as a header"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:237
msgid "Tell Orca that the current column is the one with the headers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:244
msgid "{kbd}`CapsLock+C`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:250
msgid "{kbd}`Insert+C`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:253
msgid "Reset the custom header"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:255
msgid ""
"To clear headers, double-press the command that you used to set them. This "
"removes all custom row headers or column headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:258
msgid "Fill out forms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:260
msgid ""
"In browse mode, you can read forms. In focus mode, you can fill out form "
"fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:262
msgid "Read or write"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:264
msgid "Switch between the modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:271
msgid "{kbd}`CapsLock+A`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:277
msgid "{kbd}`Insert+A`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:280
msgid "To enable **sticky focus mode**, double-press the shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:282
msgid "To enable **sticky browse mode**, triple-press the shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:284
msgid "Browse form fields"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:286
msgid ""
"In **browse** and **focus mode**, you can browse all focusable objects using "
"{kbd}`Tab` and {kbd}`Shift+Tab`. After the last form field, you exit the "
"form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:288
msgid "In **browse mode**, you can also use the following navigation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:290
msgid ""
"To navigate to a specific form field, use Structural Navigation commands for "
"{ref}`orca-structural-navigation-commands-forms`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:292
msgid ""
"To leave the form and navigate to another object, use {ref}`orca-structural-"
"navigation-commands`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:294
msgid ""
"In certain forms and applications, you can use {ref}`caret mode <orca-read-"
"documents-using-caret-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:297
msgid "Read live regions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:299
msgid ""
"A live region is a dynamically-updated portion of a web page, such as a "
"table of sports statistics, a list of current stock prices, a log from a "
"chat, or an alert displayed by the page you are reading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:301
msgid ""
"Live regions are common on the web. However, not many web pages with live "
"regions are fully accessible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:303
msgid "Browse live regions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:305
msgid "Monitor live regions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:312
msgid "{kbd}`CapsLock+Shift+\\`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:318
msgid "{kbd}`Insert+Shift+\\`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:321
msgid "Go to the next live region: {kbd}`D`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:323
msgid "Go to the previous live region: {kbd}`Shift+D`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:325
msgid "Go to last live region that made an announcement: {kbd}`Y`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:327
msgid "Review the last **nine** announcements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:334
msgid "{kbd}`CapsLock` + {kbd}`F1` through {kbd}`F9`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:340
msgid "{kbd}`Insert` + {kbd}`F1` through {kbd}`F9`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:343
msgid "Adjust live region politeness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:345
msgid ""
"Live regions have a \"politeness\" level. It tells your screen reader how "
"important the information is and when you should hear the updates in that "
"region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:347
msgid "In increasing order of importance, the politeness levels are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:349
msgid "Off"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:350
msgid "Polite"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/accessibility/orca/read-documents-and-web-pages-using-the-screen-reader.md:351
